Subject: GBA SIO: cooperative-lockstep + savestate-exactness fork delta
Series-Step: 1/19 (mgba_dual 1.6-os4)
Origin: tangobattle/mgba 2db16a6053f7da68fc485589a4426825b6341f50 (2026-07-17), MPL-2.0; carried unchanged in the hb_dual branch, original authors are credited there
요약: 한 스레드가 연결된 GBA 여럿을 번갈아 돌릴 수 있는 협력식 lockstep 케이블 + 상태 저장이 비트까지 같게 복원되도록 함(tangobattle/mgba 에서 가져옴).

The squashed delta this fork carries for tango's SIO-rollback engine
(mgba-siolink): every linked core is driven cooperatively from ONE
thread, and link snapshots must restore bit-exactly.

Lockstep driver:
- Park a player that catches the shared clock while its queue head is
  still in the future. The old code rescheduled at a non-positive
  offset — busy-waiting on another thread advancing the shared clock,
  which a single-threaded embedding does not have (netplay hard-freeze).
- Discard stale TRANSFER_STARTs: a detach aborts the transfer but
  leaves the event in surviving queues, and the same detach can promote
  the holder to clock owner; draining it then flagged a phantom
  transfer, acked a wait nobody held, and drove the finishCycle
  reschedule non-positive.
- Log-and-clamp any remaining non-positive reschedule instead of
  asserting: aborting a live session over a recoverable protocol hiccup
  is strictly worse than a clamped frame plus the host's stall guards
  and cross-peer state checks.
- Deschedule the lockstep timing event before restoring it: restoring
  onto a live driver double-listed the event and corrupted the timing
  list.

Savestate exactness (rollback restores must not fork the trajectory):
- Rebase negative CPU cycles into masterCycles when serializing: a core
  parked mid-event-batch legitimately holds cycles == nextEvent < 0,
  which GBADeserialize rejected as corruption.
- Do not fire SIO driver mode switches on deserialize: restore the
  derived link mode directly instead of re-deriving through
  GBASIOWriteRCNT, which handed the driver a spurious edge while the
  machine was half-restored.
- Serialize the transfer-completion event exactly (explicit scheduled
  bit + signed offset) instead of the legacy (SIOCNT & 0x0080) &&
  when < 0x20000 heuristic, which both dropped overdue completions and
  conjured phantom ones.
- Serialize SIOMLT_SEND: the multi-mode transmit latch was never
  stored, so a rollback resimulation could transmit a stale payload.

(cherry picked from commit 2db16a6053f7da68fc485589a4426825b6341f50)

---
diff --git a/include/mgba/internal/gba/serialize.h b/include/mgba/internal/gba/serialize.h
index 0192cd90ffee..bffc0caa6a7a 100644
--- a/include/mgba/internal/gba/serialize.h
+++ b/include/mgba/internal/gba/serialize.h
@@ -303,6 +303,7 @@ DECL_BITS(GBASerializedHWFlags2, GbpTxPosition, 4, 4);
 
 DECL_BITFIELD(GBASerializedHWFlags3, uint8_t);
 DECL_BITS(GBASerializedHWFlags3, RtcSioOutput, 0, 1);
+DECL_BIT(GBASerializedHWFlags3, SioCompleteScheduled, 1);
 
 DECL_BITFIELD(GBASerializedUnlCartFlags, uint16_t);
 DECL_BITS(GBASerializedUnlCartFlags, Type, 0, 5);
